## Services and data
{{range .Services}}
{{if eq . "postgres" -}}
- **postgres**: data lives in the `postgres_data` named volume, which survives
  `docker compose down` but not `docker compose down -v`. Back up with
  `docker compose exec postgres sh -c 'pg_dump -U "$POSTGRES_USER" "$POSTGRES_DB"' > backup.sql`.
{{else if eq . "redis" -}}
- **redis**: runs without a named volume — treat its data as ephemeral cache or
  queue state. If you need persistence, enable AOF (`--appendonly yes`) and add
  a volume.
{{else if eq . "mysql" -}}
- **mysql**: data lives in the `mysql_data` named volume, which survives
  `docker compose down` but not `docker compose down -v`. Back up with
  `docker compose exec mysql sh -c 'mysqldump -u root -p"$MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD" --all-databases' > backup.sql`.
{{else if eq . "mongo" -}}
- **mongo**: data lives in the `mongo_data` named volume, which survives
  `docker compose down` but not `docker compose down -v`. Back up with
  `docker compose exec mongo sh -c 'mongodump --archive -u "$MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME" -p "$MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD"' > backup.archive`.
{{else -}}
- **{{.}}**: <!-- TODO: dockerize has no deploy notes for this service — document its data and backup story here. -->
{{end -}}
{{end}}
